<onlyinclude>A '''knowledge ecosystem''' is a network of people, organizations, tools, practices and resources through which knowledge is produced, shared, evaluated and reused. It emphasizes interactions across boundaries rather than a single organization's collection of documents.

== Explanation ==
A university laboratory, open repository, journal, research funder and industry partner may cooperate in producing and applying findings. Their roles, incentives, access rules and shared standards affect whether knowledge travels and can be reused. Such systems can also reproduce exclusions and unreliable claims.

